---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---
<Base title="Terms of Use" description="The terms for using the FreelanceDesk website and its free invoice and quotation tools.">
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:56px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem);margin:10px 0 6px">Terms of Use</h1>
        <p style="color:var(--muted)">Website and free tools · Updated {SITE.updated}</p>

        <p>These terms cover your use of the FreelanceDesk website and its free tools, published by {SITE.company} ("we", "us"). The mobile app has its own terms inside the app. By using this website you agree to these terms.</p>

        <h2>1. The free tools</h2>
        <p>The invoice and quotation generators let you create PDF documents in your browser. Each verified account can download {SITE.freeLimit} invoices and {SITE.freeLimit} quotations for free each calendar month. We may change the free limit or the tools at any time.</p>

        <h2>2. Your content is your responsibility</h2>
        <p>You are responsible for the accuracy of every document you create, including prices, tax, dates and legal wording. The tools help you format documents. They do not give tax, legal or accounting advice. Check the rules that apply to you or ask a professional.</p>

        <h2>3. Your account</h2>
        <p>Keep your password private. You must give a real email address that you control. Creating several accounts to get around the free limit, or trying to bypass the limit by technical means, is not allowed, and we may close accounts that do.</p>

        <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>Do not use the website to break the law, to create misleading or fraudulent documents, to attack or overload the service, or to copy it or its code in bulk.</p>

        <h2>5. Availability</h2>
        <p>We try to keep the site running, but we do not promise it will always be available or error-free. The tools are provided "as is".</p>

        <h2>6. Limit of liability</h2>
        <p>To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for lost income, lost data, or other losses that come from using the website or the documents you make with it.</p>

        <h2>7. Our content</h2>
        <p>The website, its design and its articles belong to {SITE.company}. Your documents belong to you.</p>

        <h2>8. Governing law</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of Sri Lanka, without regard to conflict-of-law principles.</p>

        <h2>9. Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms. If we do, we will change the date above. Using the website after a change means you accept the new terms.</p>

        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
